WEBVTT

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.970
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.210
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.050
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.550
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.920
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.500
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.200
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Give thanks!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.410
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.550
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.820
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.990
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:31.070
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.440
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.040
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.310
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.990
Someone once said...

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.460
There's a lotus root like a roulette wheel,

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:58.760
that can taste wonderful or terrible,

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.900
depending on where the spin stops...

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.540
Roulotus!

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.240
There are whales that spew out 600 million 
yen worth of first-class ingredients

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:19.480
if the number sequences match...

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.420
Whalottery!

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.260
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:35.760
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:42.500
In order to get their hands on Meteor 
Garlic, an ingredient on Ichiryu's list,

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.910
Toriko, Coco, and Komatsu entered the 
Gourmet Casino with Match and his men.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:52.980
After winning a bundle on the general 
floor, they were ushered to the VIP area,

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.310
where the prizes are illegal ingredients.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:00.750
Then, the owner of the casino and the 
boss of the Underground Cooking World,

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.390
Livebearer, appeared before 
Toriko and the others!

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:09.760
I invite you beyond the VIP area.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:17.870
Life and Death Card Game! Gourmet Tasting!

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:24.440
Let's all bet on something more delicious!

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.240
Something better...

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:35.690
The ingredients they won on the general 
floor are all rare and valuable...

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.520
So what could be better than that?

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:19.900
Welcome to the underground VIP area.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.770
Underground VIP area...

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:29.010
Only certain select VIP guests 
are allowed to enter this room.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:32.780
Of course, you folks live 
up to those standards.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:36.180
Particularly Toriko and Coco...

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.460
I never knew tastes like this existed!

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.490
Delicious! It's delicious!

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:58.300
More! Bring me another serving right away!

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.500
W-W-What is that?!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.610
Give them back to me... Give them back!

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.010
Please!

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:10.410
Give me back my... my memories of food!

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.920
Those memories were no great shakes.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:17.520
Get him out of here.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.620
Give them back...

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:22.320
Give me back my gourmet history!

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.830
Food history?

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:25.960
Don't tell me...

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.100
The rumors are true then?!

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:32.200
They must have gambled 
with them in the casino...

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.200
Their memories of eating food...

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.170
Their history of eating... Gourmet history...

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.510
Gourmet history?!

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.680
As I'd expect from Coco of the Four Kings...

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.680
You're well informed.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:47.610
I heard about it when I was in Jiddal before,

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.580
searching for info on a certain ingredient.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.190
Oh, I see.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:57.220
So you've been to Jiddal before...

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.520
Well?

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.790
Did you find information on that ingredient?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:01.660
No.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.660
That's too bad.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.430
Incidentally, what was the ingredient?

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.000
Atom.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.170
Atom?!

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.940
The Gourmet God Acacia's Full Course Drink.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.280
I'm after that to make it part 
of my life's Full Course.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.180
Makes sense.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:27.690
It's very difficult to find 
information on that ingredient.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.020
But you may be able to get a hint

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:32.920
in the underground VIP area.

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.860
From someone's memories, you see...

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.770
Oh, good timing. Here are some 
memories being siphoned away now.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:44.570
Would you like to take a look?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.280
Our VIPs are first-class Gourmet Hunters

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.780
who always capture and eat the most 
valuable and rare ingredients,

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.380
so their brains are packed 
with delicious memories.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.950
Stop!!

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.260
My daughter's birthday!

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.760
S-Stop it...

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.900
It's too late to do anything, Toriko.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:19.670
Don't!

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:21.770
If you try to stop it now, 
it'd be dangerous for him.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:25.910
That's right. There's a good chance 
his mind would be destroyed.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:30.010
Although meals were important to him...

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:33.880
He has a close connection 
to precious anniversaries,

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.920
so if those memories disappear,

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.090
he may lose his mind anyway!

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.490
Who knows?

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:49.600
S-Stop it! Don't do this!

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.470
His memories of meals are mine now.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.580
That's too cruel!

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.010
Cruel?

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.910
He's the one who came to the Gourmet 
Casino and gambled with his Gourmet Data.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:07.620
But he lost.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.850
And that's the end result of his wager.

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:13.720
Memories are no more than 
signals sent to the brain.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.860
Tastes as well...

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:19.260
All I do is take out the 
signals for "deliciousness"

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.760
in the form of data and load 
them into another brain.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:25.030
So you can enjoy the delicious 
tastes experienced by others?!

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.500
That must be what that creepy thing 
on the back of your head is for.

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:34.710
There are many VIPs who crave 
the memories I've gathered.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.280
That's why they gamble here,

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.550
putting their own gourmet 
memories on the line.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.550
Memories are a gold mine.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:46.890
Extinct ingredients and illegal ingredients 
that were popular in the past...

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.520
With the data of their flavors,

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:53.460
it's even possible to bring back powerful 
narcotic ingredients of the past.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.360
Scum!

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:07.170
Well?

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:10.840
Do you have the courage to 
lose delicious memories?

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:11.810
Come on!

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.450
Put your memories at stake

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:17.620
and challenge me!

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:21.620
Meteor Garlic...

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:24.020
Is it one of your prizes?

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:27.060
It is indeed.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:28.690
The data of the flavor

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:31.260
is in my memory.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.770
So that's what this is about...

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.170
Old Man Ichiryu...

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.540
Whatever game it is where 
you play for memories...

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:40.010
You're on!

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:41.970
That's what I'm talking about!

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:43.910
Y-You're going to do it?!

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:47.110
Toriko-san! They may disappear!

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:50.280
Toriko-san...

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:58.460
Your memories...

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.590
All of your delicious memories...

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:02.760
Oh, dear.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.900
It's too late to back out now.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:09.230
The die has been cast.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:51.540
Welcome to the Gourmet Tasting place.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.240
Gourmet Tasting?

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.180
It's a simple game of cards.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.780
You know the game of 
concentration, don't you?

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:02.550
The game we're going to play 
is Gourmet Concentration.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.650
Now, pay attention.

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:08.320
I'll explain the rules.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.890
Listen carefully.

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:13.560
You're going to use these 
Gourmet Tasting cards.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.530
On the back is a number.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:19.230
On the front is an ingredient and a point.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:23.970
Whoever gathers the most points wins.

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.540
For example, with this card...

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:28.180
Celebeef, worth 10 points...

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.240
That's it.

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:35.080
First, the cards are randomly 
lined up face down.

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:38.220
Two cards are turned over.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:42.620
If the designs of the two cards 
don't match, the person is out.

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:47.800
Then the other person chooses two cards.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:52.300
If the two cards have the same 
picture pattern, it's a hit.

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:56.770
So it's pretty much concentration...

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:57.770
Yes.

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:00.540
But there's one big difference here.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.110
The person who gets a matching pair

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:05.110
has to eat the same food that's on the cards.

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.410
After the ingredient is devoured,

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:11.650
the person gets the number of 
points that are on the card.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:14.520
For Celebeef, that would be 10 points.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.220
So you get a match, you get to eat!

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:18.860
I love the game already!

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:20.630
Yes, however...

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.530
If the person can't eat 
all of the ingredient,

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.500
the points go to the opponent.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:31.600
On top of that, it also 
becomes the opponent's turn.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.980
So even with a match, if you can't eat 
the food, you don't get any points.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:38.910
In fact, your opponent gets those points...

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.310
That's it.

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:42.620
I see.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:46.050
And if you can't finish the 
ingredients twice in a row,

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.990
you lose right then and there.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:54.230
Also, if you don't get any pairs ten 
times in a row, you lose as well,

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:55.560
so be careful.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.400
If it's the same game as concentration,

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.270
after getting a match and 
eating the ingredient,

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:02.100
the player gets to turn over two more cards?

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:03.370
Indeed.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:06.140
But only three times in a row.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.170
If the player gets three hits and 
eats three ingredients in a row,

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:10.840
it becomes the other player's 
turn to choose two cards.

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:15.350
With these rules, everyone has the 
chance to eat many ingredients.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:16.680
I get it.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:19.580
So how many ingredients are there?

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:21.450
28 in total.

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.720
What, is that all?!

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:26.020
You say it so casually.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:28.590
But you shouldn't underestimate the game.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:32.530
You see, there are two joker ingredients.

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:34.530
Joker ingredients?

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:39.470
Yes. All challengers will have a hard 
time polishing off those ingredients.

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:41.910
But if you are able to finish it,

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:48.610
you can trade any one of your 
ingredients with your opponent's.

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:51.620
In other words, if you're able to 
finish eating the joker ingredient,

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:55.890
you can steal your opponent's 
high point value ingredients.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:56.850
Correct.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:00.360
But you still have to 
completely eat the ingredient

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.630
gotten from your opponent or it's no good.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.990
Well, the gist of it is

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.960
you match cards, eat a bunch of food,

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:10.730
and at the end, the player with 
the most points wins, right?

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:12.370
He got right to the heart of it!

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:15.270
Yes, basically, that's it.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:18.040
Now, shall we decide on 
the level of the cards?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:18.870
Level?

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:19.810
Yes.

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:24.450
Just as a restaurant has stars, 
these cards have levels.

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:29.350
The higher the level, the better the 
quality and rarity of the ingredients.

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:33.590
Although that also means eating 
more difficult ingredients, too...

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:38.560
If we're gonna do this game, we might 
as well do it with tasty ingredients.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:39.830
Good point.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:44.400
Still, the level of the cards used 
corresponds to the memories that are bet.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.670
And make no mistake, we're playing 
at the highest level, right?

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:52.310
Now then, there are many 
thousands of sets of cards.

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:56.010
Choose one and we'll use it for this game.

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:56.910
Wait a second.

00:14:57.150 --> 00:15:00.410
Can you prove that the cards don't favor you?

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:02.120
Y-Yeah!

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:03.680
No, I can't prove that.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.020
However...

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:10.960
I'm not only a chef, but also the owner 
of the Gourmet Casino and a dealer.

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:12.090
Do you understand?

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:14.860
I have pride as a gambler.

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.960
I would never stoop to cheating.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:20.970
Besides, winning through fraudulent 
means wouldn't be fun at all.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.570
Could've fooled me.

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.870
Well, shall we begin the game?

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:27.610
Toriko-san, this is just too dangerous!

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.180
He's an expert at this game!

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:35.650
If you and the others lost memories 
of food you've eaten, I...

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:36.880
I...

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:40.020
I couldn't stand it!

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:42.120
The past doesn't matter.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:46.530
We've only got our eyes on the future.

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.290
And I'm talking all the time!

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:49.600
Besides...

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:53.400
There's no way we're gonna lose, right?

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:55.070
Toriko-san...

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.870
And so...

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.210
I'm leaving it in your hands, Coco.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:05.240
In the end, you're putting it on me?!

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.650
After all of that cool talk?!

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.380
I'm entrusting you with the future.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:13.950
Oh, dear. I don't mind 
if you all participate.

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:15.920
Really?!

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:18.490
In that case, I'll get in on this, too.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:20.690
Except not as a player...

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:21.990
I'm the dealer.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:25.160
This is the sumo ring of the 
Underground Cooking World.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:27.400
Least you can do is let me deal.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.330
I-In that case,

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:33.100
I'll prepare the matched ingredients 
so they're tasty enough to eat!

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:34.640
That's my role!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.740
Of course, I'll do the eatin'!

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:38.780
And Coco here will match 'em up!

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:40.610
Yes. I'll choose the cards.

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:45.920
Fine with me.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:48.750
You're all welcome at my table!

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:52.290
Alright, this game of Gourmet Concentration,

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:55.060
Gourmet Tasting, is about to begin!

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:56.690
They've got an announcer!

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:59.030
After all, it's a fun game,

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.560
so that adds even more excitement!

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:03.000
It's our boss, the boss of the 
Underground Cooking World,

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.140
Livebearer-sama, and challenging him

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:06.840
are two of the Four Kings, Toriko and Coco,

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:08.940
as well as Chef Komatsu from Hotel Gourmet!

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.880
Livebearer, are you okay all alone?

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:13.040
Of course.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:16.580
I've always played on my own.

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:19.820
And, by the by, my record 
is 214 wins and no losses.

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:25.190
I've cleaned out the brains of every 
single one of my guests up to now.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:27.790
Word to the wise...

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:32.260
You'd do well not to confuse us with 
any of the guests you've played before.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:34.760
Is that right?

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.730
You're quite confident, too.

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:39.300
Where does that confidence come from?

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:40.940
You'll find out soon enough.

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:42.470
Let's decide who goes first.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.470
We'll do a coin toss.

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:48.540
What's it gonna be, heads or tails?

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:53.850
As this is the Underworld, I'll be tails.

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:56.180
Coco, you okay with heads?

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:57.220
Neither.

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:01.020
Neither. That's my call.

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:03.290
Coco-san?

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.030
Then here I go...

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:11.930
Right now,

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:14.270
the coin that will decide the players' fates

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:16.040
is spinning through the air!

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.440
It was an energetic flip...

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:21.040
...that landed on top of the table!

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:22.840
And now it's rolling!

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:26.410
What's it gonna be ?! Heads?! Or tails?!

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.820
I-It's tails!

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:36.290
Whoa! What's this?!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:38.560
The coin righted itself!

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:40.460
What is that?!

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.330
Neither heads nor tails.

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:45.330
Oh!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.030
It's standing!

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:50.300
The coin is standing on its side!

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:53.970
What an eventful way to start the 
game! Who could've predicted this?!

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:56.840
I mean, it <i>was</i> predicted!

00:18:57.080 --> 00:19:00.650
Even though I flipped the coin 
normally, it went like that...

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:03.580
Coco-san, that was too awesome for words!

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.320
I guess we'll go first.

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:06.820
Be my guest.

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:10.660
This is fun already. Certainly, you're 
different from all my previous guests.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:12.560
Call out your numbers.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:14.330
I'll flip the cards over.

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:16.060
Number eight.

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:19.600
The Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team is going first!

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:23.270
The sourness of superb apples 
with the sweetness of cherries!

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:25.170
We open with Cherry Apples!

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:27.710
Cherry Apples! That's a 
high class ingredient!

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:29.710
If I flip over one more Cherry Apple,

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:31.810
we'll get ten points.

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:33.780
No way is it gonna be that easy.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:37.020
It's gonna start with a series of "outs".

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:41.150
But as the cards flip, he's gotta check 
their point value and ingredient.

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:43.760
Number 29.

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:51.630
Cherry Apples!

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:54.330
A hit on the very first try!

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:55.630
Oh, my...

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:58.500
Again, too awesome for words!

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.510
Please eat these Cherry Apples.

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:06.740
Eating time has come early for 
the Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team!

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:08.610
Over to you, Toriko.

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:09.910
Leave it to me!

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:11.750
I don't need any seasoning for this!

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:14.820
Nope! They're tasty as is!

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:20.460
I give thanks for all of 
this world's great bounty!

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:29.170
Delicious!

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:35.140
The Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team gets ten points!

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:38.540
Well, shall we keep going?

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:39.680
Yeah!

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:41.610
A coincidence?

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:44.680
No, I don't think so.

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:48.780
This man knows which cards match.

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:53.020
This looks to become my first 
fun game in a long while.

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:08.240
In those younger days,

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:10.140
No matter how you chased them,

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:14.710
The sky-spanning rainbows got away

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:18.010
After that, time passed

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:20.520
Were you able to grasp

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:25.150
The rainbow by the name of dreams then?

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:28.860
When it comes to a new challenge,

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:34.100
You turn into a coward,

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:39.570
But your chance ain't gonna wait on you,

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:44.440
So now's the time!

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:52.110
Bet those tears and that kindness

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:56.350
Will light up tomorrow

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:59.420
That's right, rainbows are 
all the more beautiful

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:03.260
Because we can't catch 'em

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:07.730
Today's Gourmet Tasting Lecture!

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:09.360
I'm your newscaster, Tina.

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:12.130
Gourmet Tasting has begun at last!

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:14.370
In this segment, I'll give you 
a heaping helping of commentary

00:22:14.370 --> 00:22:17.500
on today's game and its important points!

00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:22.340
To be honest, I'd like to 
be the game's commentator...

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:25.910
...but since the casino isn't 
a member nation of IGO,

00:22:25.910 --> 00:22:28.550
it's out of the question for 
me, so nothing I can do...

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:31.050
Pardon me!

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:35.350
So the Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team went first.

00:22:35.350 --> 00:22:37.160
Amazingly, on the first try,

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:40.590
Coco pulled off the remarkable feat 
of matching two Cherry Apple cards.

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:42.830
Then, Toriko did a great job eating them!

00:22:43.230 --> 00:22:45.860
Toriko's team got ten points!

00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:50.670
Here's today's cool point!

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:55.470
Actually, ten is the lowest number 
of points you can get for a match.

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:58.310
In other words, it's quite possible 
for the other side to catch up!

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:01.380
How will Livebearer do on his turn?!

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:03.150
I'm feeling a heaping helping of excitement!

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:05.150
And now, on to our next segment!

00:23:07.310 --> 00:23:10.720
Electromagnetic waves versus supernatural powers. Coco of the Four Heavenly Kings gets to flex his skills.

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:13.890
Meanwhile, Toriko faces down a mountain of pudding!?

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:16.790
Dead Heat! Coco vs. Livebearer!

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:18.870
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
